    "top_frame": "The offense couldn't finish when it mattered late.",
    "what_this_means": "That's what this game came down to. They scratched out runners in the eighth and tenth innings. Had genuine chances with two outs, bases loaded, the game within reach. Volpe tied it in the ninth, which should have been the spark. Instead, Detroit scored four in the eleventh while Warren and the relievers held Detroit to two runs through 5.1 and 4.2 innings of shutdown work. The math was simple: good pitching, wasted opportunities, and now they're four back. Inconsistency isn't a mood. It's the ceiling.",
